Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Record an audit trail of Redfish requests

Nothing recorded who changed what through Redfish: a successful reset,
alert submission or subscription left no trace at the default log
level, and the debug level printed credentials.

 * routing.hpp: write one audit record when a state-changing or
   refused request completes. The hook sits below route lookup, so all
   routes are covered.
 * http_connection.hpp, http2_connection.hpp: record requests refused
   for missing or bad credentials, which never reach the router. Stop
   logging the client address with each request.
 * authentication.hpp: stop logging the Authorization header, cookie
   values, the Basic user name and the client address.
 * webserver_run.cpp: record service start.

The record format and the allow-list of logged fields live in
redfish_audit.hpp and redfish_audit_hook.hpp, which the build copies
into include/ from redfish-audit/.

